So to get automationPrUrl non-null in a test: mock `cli_execute_command` so that the command `gh pr list --head test/PROJ-6618 --json url --jq ".[0].url"` returns 'https://github.com/org/repo/pull/7'. Then createPullRequest returns {success:true, prUrl: that}. Then in action, feature PR found → label update → injectAutomationPrLink reads pr_feature_update.md; if it contains content without the URL → file_write appends. I'll capture file_write and assert the appended link line.

Plan:
1. Extract `injectAutomationPrLink` helper (CC ~5) from updateFeaturePR.
2. Fix hasA11yWarnings CC (extract hasWarningsArray, direct access results[i].a11y_warnings).
3. Add action-flow test "injects automation PR link into pr_feature_update.md" covering injectAutomationPrLink + updateFeaturePR true branch.

updateFeaturePR after extraction:
```js
function updateFeaturePR(featureScm, ticketKey, featureOwner, featureRepo, passed, labelPassed, labelFailed, workingDir, automationPrUrl, result) {
   var featurePR = findFeaturePR(ticketKey, featureScm, featureOwner, featureRepo);
   if (!featurePR) {
       return;
   }
   updateFeaturePRLabelWithScm(featureScm, featurePR.number, passed, labelPassed, labelFailed);
   // Inject automation PR URL into feature update markdown if present
   injectAutomationPrLink(workingDir, ticketKey, automationPrUrl);
   updateFeaturePRBodyWithScm(featureScm, featurePR.number, workingDir, result, ticketKey);
}
```

injectAutomationPrLink CC: 1 + if(!url) + try/catch + || + && = 5. Covered by new test → 5 ✓.

